{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546369-what-was-the-reason-for-all-the-hunter-the-reckoning-revised-edition-hate","id":1546369,"title":"What was the reason for all the Hunter the Reckoning (Revised Edition) hate?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-24T21:37:22-08:00","id":1546369,"title":"What was the reason for all the Hunter the Reckoning (Revised Edition) hate?","content":"I been looking at Hunter the Reckoning topic on this forum, and found a lot of people seem to hate the gamline. I thought a people love it, since there seem to be a hated for HtR 5th edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T11:37:55-08:00","id":1546400,"title":"","content":"Two big reasons I've seen: It wasn't Hunters Hunted as its own gameline, or it wasn't people's image of Hunters Hunted (ordinary mortals taking on the supernatural without powers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T12:05:38-08:00","id":1546401,"title":"","content":"Yeah. For all of the digital ink spilled, flame wars waged, and so on, it really did come down to &quot;it wasn't Hunters Hunted.&quot;<br /> <br /> Reckoning certainly had it's own problems (the art, a few important mechanics that were buggy or poorly explained, etc.) but nothing particularly more glaring than other WoD games; especially when you take into account things getting worked out over time in supplements. First impressions matter, but they don't explain the response.<br /> <br /> This is also why there's still plenty of hate for H5. H5 is also not Hunters Hunted. H5 makes the Hunters Hunted groups bad guys for the brand new Driven Hunters. So it not only introduced an entirely new style of Hunter (even if just a rip from Hunter the Vigil with some of Free League's Alien RPG sprinkled on), but actively made the groups people used to love playing as unplayable antagonists.<br /> <br /> That said, there are plenty of HtR 1e fans here too. But we tend to be less vocal because it's obviously not the style of game most WoD or CofD wanted given the enduring popularity of Hunters Hunted in comparison, and the general positive acclaim towards Hunter the Vigil as being what the majority of fans wanted. HtR 1e fans tend to hate on H5 too, but it's also for the same reasons that HH fans do: a whole new style of hunter with the old style removed from play. Plus we get the additional salt in the wound of H5 keeping the HtR branding despite being a radical departure from the previous edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-26T11:53:29-08:00","id":1546425,"title":"","content":"It's almost impressive the way H5 managed to piss off both HH fans AND HtR fans, by satisfying neither. It doesn't have the cool powers or the years of lore development of HtR. And it positions the new OC Driven hunters as unambiguously good, at the expense of HH's established hunter orgs.<br /> <br /> Like, unless you were going to just create Hunter: The Vigil again (but in WoD), and have one gameline that services both low power and high power hunters, H5 was inevitably going to dissatisfy one or the other.<br /> <br /> As it stands, Paradox somehow managed to alienate BOTH segments of the Classic WoD (H)unter fandom at once. Good job. *Slow Clap*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-26T13:06:18-08:00","id":1546426,"title":"","content":"Not to try to start anything, but the &quot;low power vs high power&quot; was never really the issue. The issue is diversity vs. single style. HH (and HtV) have a wide range of options from people that witnessed the supernatural but know nothing and are trying to do something about it, all the way up to a hunter group that's literally VtM vampires trying to be &quot;good&quot; people via using their powers for monster hunting. What HtR did was make a game all about the Imbued. While explained in-universe to a reasonable level if you get far enough into the game, the core book first impression has all this preachy caveats about who is and isn't a valid person to get Imbued because the game wants to focus on &quot;normal everyday&quot; folks and not have celebrities or highly trained black ops agents, or whatever being the kinds of people that fill the ranks of the Imbued.<br /> <br /> H5 exists in a very weird middle ground. The Driven are more varied in many ways than the Imbued, but then have all of these artificial feeling limits placed on them like how you can't be Driven and join an Org, only join up with small cells of like-minded Driven that eschew any sort of larger organizational power.<br /> <br /> HH gave a lot of very flavorful options, but because it was always something built up in supplements HH play never felt fully supported in the books.<br /> <br /> HtR 1e gave a very focused game that supports it's themes fairly well, but that only works if that's the game you want.<br /> <br /> HtV gave a lot of options but importantly hit the sweet spot of supporting lots of different styles of play because it had the room to do so as a full game line of its own instead of a series of supplements.<br /> <br /> H5 tries to include all of it to the detriment of itself in every way. The flavor of the Orgs is sabotaged by being off limits to players. The focus of the Imbued is sabotaged by the lack of coherent point to the Driven beyond fulfilling an urban fantasy niche. The toolkit of the Vigil is sabotaged by the intense demand for all Driven to be low tier cells. Thus it has so little appeal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-27T02:32:40-08:00","id":1546445,"title":"","content":"<i>The Hunters Hunted</i> was very popular when first released, but actually would have a problem if spun into an entire game line; simply put, mundane hunters are, in general terms, less interesting than the monsters they are hunting. To get around this, a game focused on hunters needs a strong conceptual hook, which became the basis of the original <i>Hunter: the Reckoning</i>. I think there were a number of legitimate issues that readers had with the game in its first incarnation - the severe mismatch between art and text is one, as was the notion that it was a good idea to have supplements which were, for the most part, works of fiction. But the core concept, that of the Imbued being mysterious granted powers to fight monsters, was a strong one, and I understand why people liked the game, even though I was never personally interested in playing it. <br /> <br /> &quot;Fifth edition&quot; meanwhile, just doesn't really present any reason for existing. It feels like there was a managerial decision to make a hunter game, and no-one working on the product had any passion or, indeed, vision for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-27T07:45:35-08:00","id":1546452,"title":"","content":"So a bit of history, when Hunter the Reckoning was first announced back in 1998, people were initially lead to believe that they would be playing non-supernatural Hunters. Just regular folk out hunting monsters. Basically, everyone was expecting a game like Hunters Hunted, just designed as a fully supported splat. Then when the game released in 1999, there was the reveal that the Hunters were supernaturally imbued. That came as a fairly big surprise (even right up to the release, the truth about the Imbued had been kept completely quiet by White Wolf). <br /> <br /> There was also a major PR debacle as well. Around the time Hunter was getting ready for release, White Wolf released a press statement saying that the company had just been sold to a new owner. Some authors (who were in on the joke) were talking about how they'd just been fired, but quite a few freelance authors had no idea what was going on and thought they had just lost their jobs. Links to the new owner lead to a weird conservative/conspiracy laden website. Of course, then a week later White Wolf revealed that it was all just a PR stunt to build hype for Hunter, but a lot of White Wolf fans were kind of upset about the whole thing and, coupled with the fact that Hunters were Imbued rather than regular people, it kind of had a negative impact on the way Hunter the Reckoning was viewed by a lot of the fanbase.<br /> <br /> Not too long later, it was (sort of) revealed that Hunter (and by extension the rest of the World of Darkness) was linked to Exalted, and that ticked a certain segment of the fanbase off again. Many of the &quot;mature gamers&quot; didn't like the idea of a &quot;power-gaming anime RPG&quot; having anything to do with their ultra serious gothic punk horror gameline. This was quickly walked back in Exalted in the ST guide where the authors said, &quot;No no, Exalted could be the pre-history of <i>a</i> World of Darkness, not necessarily <i>the</i> World of Darkness.&quot; But for quite a few people, this was another strike against Hunter.<br /> <br /> So understand that HtR was pretty controversial at release.<br /> <br /> Still, HtR gained a decent fanbase, and this was helped by the release of some very solid video games on the X-Box and PS2. But after White Wolf moved to the new World of Darkness, that was it for HtR. It was left to languish and never received a 20th Anniversary edition or anything.<br /> <br /> When the new Hunter the Reckoning 5th edition was announced, the old Hunter fans were stoked. But what they got was not Hunter the Reckoning, but rather a new edition of Hunters Hunted. The Imbued were nowhere to be seen. A lot of Hunter fans were like, &quot;Wait a second, Hunter 5th edition isn't a new edition of Hunter the Reckoning, it's a completely different gameline that just shares the name and the theme of fighting monsters with the old edition.&quot; As a result, many of those old-school Hunter the Reckoning fans (fairly or unfairly) panned the book kinda hard.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the 5th edition of Hunter the Reckoning is what people were originally expecting Hunter the Reckoning to be like back in late 1999 just before the game released. But HtR has had two decades with its identity completely tied to the concept of the Imbued, that removing it kind of ticked off a portion of the people who had become fans of the gameline and were expecting a new edition of <i>that</i> not a different game altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-27T09:59:12-08:00","id":1546454,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify, we released a bunch of promos that indicated that the HtR hunters had some sort of supernatural bonus. The two main pieces of ad and poster art showed a Buffy-esque character, a supernaturally enhanced character in pop culture, and an Ahnold-resembling guy with energy swashes up from his shoulders like wings. I can't speak for our ability to push out info at that time, or how directly it was stated, but the reality is that game companies then did not have the same connection to the fans in a variety of social media and so were still used to putting out info leading up to a release by using older, less transparent messaging. What I <i>can </i>say is that there was no internal desire to pretend the Imbued were HH style hunters, and if the fact that they had powers wasn't directly stated until the launch in order to have a similar impact as these new Hunters had on WoD as a setting, it wasn't hidden either.<br /> <br /> Now as for that whole &quot;WW was sold&quot; thing, I'm of two minds. Back then, I was against it, because I'm not a fan of hoax marketing - you'll note that Onyx has never done that - but at the same time, I mean, Really? We sold out to evangelicals? And as noted: &quot;Links to the new owner led to a weird conservative/conspiracy laden website.&quot; Like I said, not a marketing campaign I had anything to do with, but the ad team did leave enough breadcrumbs that folks should have been suspicious of the unlikeliness of that whole scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-27T15:24:58-08:00","id":1546459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546369-what-was-the-reason-for-all-the-hunter-the-reckoning-revised-edition-hate?p=1546452#post1546452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a bit of history, when Hunter the Reckoning was first announced back in 1998, people were initially lead to believe that they would be playing non-supernatural Hunters. Just regular folk out hunting monsters. Basically, everyone was expecting a game like Hunters Hunted, just designed as a fully supported splat. Then when the game released in 1999, there was the reveal that the Hunters were supernaturally imbued. That came as a fairly big surprise (even right up to the release, the truth about the Imbued had been kept completely quiet by White Wolf).</div> </div> </div> </div>Have been around at the time as a fan, the amount of fans convincing themselves of what HtR was going to be that was just mutually reinforcing speculation with no actual evidence was kind of astounding.<br /> <br /> It was also pretty weird to see how, in 96 and 97, people were complaining that Hunters in the WoD were <i>too supernatural</i> because HH and later supplements kept introducing hunting groups with powers and &quot;just regular folk out hunting monsters&quot; was never really represented in the books.<br /> <br /> When early HtR promo stuff made it clear that the game was going to focus on &quot;normal folks&quot; everyone just assumed that meant &quot;no powers&quot; instead of things like, &quot;not being a member of a secretive government agency or an ancient mystic cult.&quot; There was the really weird period where people kept insisting that the heart of HH was &quot;normal non-powered hunters,&quot; no matter how many citations to Numina and etc. that HH and supplements were constantly putting into the WoD. <br /> <br /> HtR wasn't controversial because fans were &quot;lead to believe&quot; anything. It was because a few loud fans convinced themselves their pet theories on the game were accurate, and went around spreading those theories as if fact confirmed by WW when they just flat out weren't. Some of them were even shot down on the old WW BBS and that didn't stop people from treating fan rumors as official statements from the company.<br /> <br /> There's just a frustrating amount of revisionism around what happened that always seems to be around justifying how it's anyone's fault other than the people that did all the stoking of fans with zero actual real information from WW to base it on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-28T11:38:25-08:00","id":1546471,"title":"","content":"I'm still kind of sad that writer Adam Tinworth wasn't able to do his idea for Victorian Age Hunter, which would have been almost entirely about people akin to Van Helsing's group in Dracula, Sherlock Holmes, and Carnacki.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-28T12:44:12-08:00","id":1546473,"title":"","content":"I would love to see a Victorian Age Hunter game someday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}